==================================================
CURRENT PONS V2 LAUNCH-GATE STATUS
==================================================

The repository's current integration snapshot records that public Pons v2 launches are presently gated.

Therefore:

THE EXISTENCE OF A LAUNCH FUNCTION DOES NOT MEAN THE CREATOR MAY USE IT.

The integration must call:

canLaunch(address)

immediately before preparing a live launch.

The creator address used in the manifest must be the address checked.

If:

canLaunch(creator) = false

then:

BLOCK.

Do not generate a transaction intended to bypass the gate.

Do not substitute another wallet solely to defeat a permission restriction.

Do not infer launch authority from a previously successful experiment.

Launch permission is a runtime fact.

==================================================
CAN DOES NOT MEAN MAY
==================================================

This creates two distinct gates.

PROTOCOL GATE

canLaunch(address)

and

PONS $101 HUMAN GATE

human authorization.

Both must pass.

The sequence is:

PROTOCOL SAYS CAN LAUNCH

↓

PONS $101 PREFLIGHT PASSES

↓

HUMAN REVIEWS

↓

HUMAN DECIDES WHETHER TO LAUNCH

The protocol's:

TRUE

does not mean:

EXECUTE.

It only means the protocol currently permits the address.

